---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import QuickAnswer from '../../../components/QuickAnswer.astro';
import LastVerified from '../../../components/LastVerified.astro';
import SourceList from '../../../components/SourceList.astro';
import RelatedGuides from '../../../components/RelatedGuides.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../../../components/SectionHeader.astro';
import CTASection from '../../../components/CTASection.astro';
import AdsterraNativeBanner from '../../../components/AdsterraNativeBanner.astro';
import AdsterraBanner300x250 from '../../../components/AdsterraBanner300x250.astro';
import { sourceUrls } from '../../../data/sources';

const title = 'DragonSword Awakening Beginner Guide — First Hours & Combat Basics';
const description = 'A practical DragonSword Awakening beginner guide covering first-hours progression, tag combat, early teams, exploration, Cooking, Familiars, and safe upgrade habits.';
const canonical = 'https://dragonswordguide.com/guides/beginner/';
const article = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Article', headline: title, description, mainEntityOfPage: canonical, datePublished: '2026-08-08', dateModified: '2026-08-13', publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'DragonSword Guide' } };
const sources = [{ label: 'Official Steam store page', href: sourceUrls.steam, note: 'supports Orbis, companions, Cooking, Familiars, Status Ailments, Signal Skills and 19 Heroes.' }];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} ogType="article" schema={[article]}>
  <div class="shell page-wrap"><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'DragonSword Guide', href: '/' }, { label: 'Guides', href: '/guides/beginner/' }, { label: 'Beginner Guide' }]} /><article><header class="article-header"><p class="eyebrow">Guide · Getting started</p><h1>DragonSword Awakening Beginner Guide</h1><LastVerified date="August 13, 2026" /></header>
    <QuickAnswer title="Learn the combat loop before spending materials."><p>Start by understanding Active Skills, Status Ailments, Signal Skills and team switching. Build one functional three-Hero team, explore at your pace, and keep limited upgrade materials for characters you have actually tested.</p></QuickAnswer>
    <div class="article-body"><SectionHeader title="First-hours checklist" description="A low-regret route for a new save." /><ul class="checklist"><li>Complete the opening tutorials and read the combat prompts.</li><li>Practice dodge, camera control and switching before chasing damage.</li><li>Learn how Active Skills apply or use Status Ailments.</li><li>Use Signal Skills after the relevant ailment setup.</li><li>Keep one functional three-Hero team before splitting resources.</li><li>Follow story progression, then return for caves, cellars and side content.</li><li>Cook when you have ingredients; treat recipes as part of progression, not decoration.</li><li>Experiment with Familiars and note what each one changes for your route.</li><li>Install the game on an SSD; Steam lists an SSD as strictly required for an optimal experience.</li></ul>
      <h2>What to do first</h2><p>DragonSword: Awakening introduces an open world, companions and tag-team combat at the same time. Resist the urge to optimize every system immediately. Your first useful milestone is a team that can reliably create a Status Ailment and convert it into a Signal Skill.</p>
      <h2>Understand the three-Hero combat flow</h2><p>Use an Active Skill, watch for the Status Ailment it creates, then switch into the Hero whose Signal Skill can capitalize on the opening. The official store description supports Heroes, Status Ailments, Signal Skills and Switching Signals; it does not define one mandatory rotation for every team.</p>
      <h2>Build a functional early team</h2><p>Think in roles rather than a tier list: a setup Hero, a connector who can exploit the status state, and a finisher. Team order matters because switching is part of the combat language, not just a way to escape danger. Use the <a href="/teams/">Teams hub</a> for the framework; do not treat it as a “best team” ranking.</p>
      <h2>Understand builds before chasing meta</h2><p>A build describes how one Hero or combat approach uses roles, skills and resources; team composition describes how multiple Heroes connect their effects. Runes and Karma belong in that broader resource discussion, but exact best-in-slot choices remain <strong>NOT_YET_VERIFIED</strong>. Continue to the <a href="/builds/">Builds framework</a> and <a href="/systems/runes/">Rune guide</a> when you are ready for those systems.</p>
      <h2>Exploration and map</h2><p>Orbis includes meadows, watchtower cellars, deep seas, caves and dungeons. Mark places you cannot finish yet and return after story or system progress; use the <a href="/map/">Map reference</a> for the current verified boundary instead of assuming every location has been mapped.</p>
      <h2>Multiplayer and co-op</h2><p>Steam lists Online Co-op, while the current guide separates confirmed activities from story and open-world questions that remain unverified. See <a href="/multiplayer/">Multiplayer and Co-op</a> for the primary-source boundary.</p>
      <h2>What should a new player prioritize?</h2><p>Use a low-regret decision framework: learn the combat systems, understand the current roster, test how a Hero fits your team, and verify a resource before committing heavily. This guide does not name a first Hero to awaken, a strongest starter or an optimal progression route.</p>
      <AdsterraNativeBanner />
      <h2>Early mistakes to avoid</h2><ul><li>Do not spend every rare material before testing a Hero.</li><li>Do not treat an unverified community tier list as official data.</li><li>Do not assume story or open-world co-op from the store’s Online Co-op label.</li><li>Do not skip the SSD requirement when troubleshooting performance; see the <a href="/system-requirements/">official PC requirements</a>.</li></ul>
      <AdsterraBanner300x250 />
      <h2>Where to go next</h2><p>Continue with the <a href="/guides/combat-system/">Combat System</a>, then choose the page that matches your question: <a href="/characters/">Characters</a>, <a href="/teams/">Teams</a>, <a href="/builds/">Builds</a>, <a href="/systems/runes/">Runes</a>, <a href="/map/">Map</a>, <a href="/multiplayer/">Multiplayer</a> or the <a href="/roadmap/">Roadmap</a>.</p>
    </div><SourceList sources={sources} /><RelatedGuides links={[{ label: 'Combat System', href: '/guides/combat-system/' }, { label: 'PC Requirements', href: '/system-requirements/' }, { label: 'Characters', href: '/characters/' }, { label: 'Teams', href: '/teams/' }, { label: 'Builds', href: '/builds/' }, { label: 'Runes', href: '/systems/runes/' }, { label: 'Map', href: '/map/' }, { label: 'Multiplayer', href: '/multiplayer/' }, { label: 'Roadmap', href: '/roadmap/' }]} /><CTASection title="Ready for the combat loop?" primaryHref="/guides/combat-system/" primaryLabel="Read Combat System" secondaryHref="/multiplayer/" secondaryLabel="See Multiplayer" /></article></div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .page-wrap { padding: 1.25rem 0 2rem; } .article-header { max-width: 820px; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; } .eyebrow { color: var(--accent-light); font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; } h1, h2 { line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.04em; } h1 { max-width: 760px; font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 7vw, 5rem); margin: 0 0 0.7rem; } h2 { font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 3vw, 2rem); margin: 2.8rem 0 0.75rem; } .article-body { max-width: 760px; } .article-body p, li { color: var(--muted-strong); } .checklist { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0.65rem 2rem; padding-left: 1.1rem; } li { padding-left: 0.25rem; } @media (max-width: 650px) { .checklist { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
